Copyright (c) 2026 996agency. All rights reserved.

Beekiri CMS ("Beekiri" or "the Software") is free to use. This license explains
what you may do with it, and the few things you may not do. It is written in
plain language on purpose. "You" means the person or organisation using the
Software; "996agency" is the owner of the Software.


1. FREE TO USE — FOR EVERYONE, FOREVER

   You may download, install and use Beekiri free of charge:

   - on as many websites as you like;
   - for yourself, for your company, or for your clients;
   - for personal, non-profit and commercial projects;
   - on your own computer, your own server, or with any hosting provider.

   You never have to pay for Beekiri itself. 996agency will not start charging
   for a version of the Software you have already received under this license.


2. BUILD WITH IT

   You may freely:

   a) Create themes. Write your own themes, change any theme, and use the themes
      that ship with Beekiri as a starting point for your own.

   b) Create extensions. Write your own extensions that add features to
      Beekiri.

   c) Share or sell your work. Your themes and extensions belong to you. You may
      give them away or sell them under any terms you choose, as long as they do
      not contain the Beekiri core (see section 4).

   d) Build websites for others. Design, build, host and maintain Beekiri
      websites for clients and charge for that work.

   e) Use your content. The content you create and the websites Beekiri
      generates are yours. Public websites do not need to show any Beekiri
      branding.


3. CHANGES TO THE CORE

   The "core" is everything in the Software other than themes and extensions:
   the admin, the API, the setup wizard, the installer, the updater and the
   default extensions shipped with Beekiri.

   You may change the core for websites you run or build, for example to fix a
   problem. Those changes are at your own risk: core updates may replace them,
   and 996agency does not support modified installations. You may not
   distribute a changed core (see section 4).


4. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   a) No rebranding. Do not remove, replace, hide or change the Beekiri name,
      the Beekiri logo, or the copyright and license notices in the admin, the
      sign-in screen, the setup wizard, the installer or the update screens.
      ("White-labelling" Beekiri is not allowed.)

   b) No clones. Do not publish, sell or offer the Software, or a copy or
      changed version of it, as your own product or under another name. Do not
      use the Software, or substantial parts of its code, to build a competing
      content management system or website builder.

   c) No redistribution of the core. Do not share or sell the core, changed or
      unchanged, except by pointing people to the official Beekiri downloads.
      Hosting providers may install and run unmodified official releases for
      their customers, with all branding intact (see section 5).

   d) No bypassing paid licenses. Do not remove, disable or work around the
      license checks for paid themes or other paid items from the Beekiri Hub,
      and do not share paid items with people who did not buy them.


5. HOSTING PROVIDERS

   Hosting companies, agencies and platforms may offer Beekiri to their
   customers — for example as a one-click install or a managed service — using
   unmodified official releases with all Beekiri branding and notices intact.
   They may not present Beekiri as their own software.


6. PAID THEMES AND ITEMS

   Beekiri is free. Some themes and other items in the Beekiri Hub are paid.
   Each paid item comes with its own license, shown when you buy it. Unless
   that license says otherwise, a paid theme may be used on one local, one
   staging and one production website that share the same owner email address.


7. TRADEMARKS

   "Beekiri", the Beekiri logo, the bee mark and the names of Beekiri's own
   features are trademarks of 996agency. This license does not grant any
   rights to use them beyond what TRADEMARKS.md allows.


8. ENDING THIS LICENSE

   If you break this license, your right to use the Software ends. If you fix
   the problem within 30 days of being told about it, your rights are
   restored. Sections 9 and 10 continue to apply after the license ends.


9. NO WARRANTY

   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
